# Cursor AI Rules for Epi4Ab Project on Leonardo HPC

## HPC System Context
This project runs on Leonardo HPC (distributed supercomputing system at CINECA).

### System-Specific Commands
- Use `module load` to load software modules (e.g., `module load python/3.11.7`)
- SLURM job submission: Use `sbatch` or `srun` for jobs
- Python environments: Activate with `source venv/bin/activate` (not conda activate)
- File paths:
  - Work: `/leonardo_work/AIFAC_F01_302/`
  - Scratch (fast): `/leonardo_scratch/fast/AIFAC_F01_302/`
  - Scratch (large): `/leonardo_scratch/large/userexternal/knaung00/`
  - Home: `/leonardo/home/userexternal/knaung00/`

### Command Execution Differences
- Always use `bash -lc` wrapper for complex commands
- Check module availability before assuming tools exist: `module avail`
- Some tools may require SLURM job submission (not interactive execution)
- Network access may be limited (affects web API calls)
- Use absolute paths when possible (multiple workspace roots)

### Testing and Debugging
- Test antibody detection on problematic PDBs: 3N85, 6B0N
- Verify all three labels (0, 1, 2) are generated
- Check label distribution using inspect_labels.py
- Log antibody detection results for debugging

### Project Structure
- Data processing: `data_processing/epi4ab_pipeline.py`
- Model evaluation: `interface_prediction/model/testing_function.py`
- SLURM scripts: `slurm/*.sbatch`
- Processed data: `/leonardo_scratch/fast/AIFAC_F01_302/epi4ab/processed/`

